      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i never really lifted weights before but i want to start getting stronger. can u make me a simple 4 week program focusing on the main stuff like squats, bench, and deadlifts? just looking for a basic linear progression thing to get started.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A simple linear progression program for beginners focusing on the big three—squats, bench press, and deadlifts—is a fantastic starting point! You'll want to start light, focusing on perfect form before trying to lift heavy. For the next four weeks, aim to add a small amount of weight (like 2.5-5 lbs) to the bar each week for each main lift, while keeping the reps consistent. Remember to warm up thoroughly before you start, as proper technique is more important than how much you lift right now. Good luck with your new strength journey!",
