    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds okay but can u actually give me a specific schedule? like what days should i do these and how many sets/reps for each one? also sometimes i feel super drained after lifting so any tips for that part?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A schedule of 3 days a week, allowing for rest days in between, is perfect for a beginner. You could do a structure like Monday (Lower Body/Squat Focus), Wednesday (Upper Body/Bench Focus), and Friday (Full Body/Deadlift Focus), with 3-4 sets of 5-8 repetitions for your main lifts. For the heavy days, focus on good recovery; don't skip sleep, and make sure you're eating enough protein to help your muscles repair themselves. If you feel drained, it might be that your body is still adapting to the stress, which is normal when starting out.",
